  "prompt": "You are the dispatcher preparing the load sheet for a light business jet. Arms are inches aft of the datum.\n\n**Load**\n\n| Item | Weight (lb) | Arm (in) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Basic empty weight | 9,850 | 312.4 |\n| Crew (2 × 190 lb) | 380 | 128.0 |\n| Passengers, club seats (4 × 185 lb) | 740 | 335.0 |\n| Passengers, aft bench (2 × 185 lb) | 370 | 372.0 |\n| Aft baggage | 350 | 455.0 |\n\n**Fuel**\n- Ramp fuel 660 US gal of Jet-A at 6.75 lb/US gal\n- Taxi burn 200 lb; planned trip burn 2,600 lb\n- Fuel moment table from the flight manual (moment ÷ 1000, in·lb, at 6.75 lb/gal); interpolate linearly in moment between rows:\n\n| US gal | 0 | 100 | 200 | 300 | 400 | 500 | 600 | 700 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Moment/1000 | 0.0 | 214.7 | 426.6 | 634.8 | 839.7 | 1041.2 | 1239.3 | 1436.4 |\n\n**Limits**\n- LEMAC 288.0 in; MAC 80.0 in\n- CG envelope, all weights: 15.0 % to 32.0 % MAC\n- Maximum takeoff weight 16,600 lb; maximum landing weight 15,200 lb\n\n**Report**\n1. Takeoff weight (lb) and CG (%MAC)\n2. Planned landing weight (lb) and CG (%MAC)\n3. Whether takeoff is within all the limits above (true/false)\n4. Whether the planned landing is within all the limits above (true/false)\n\nShow your working. End with a single JSON object in a ```json code block, with exactly these keys, plain numbers and JSON booleans:\n\n```json\n{\"takeoff_weight_lb\": 0, \"takeoff_cg_pct_mac\": 0, \"landing_weight_lb\": 0, \"landing_cg_pct_mac\": 0, \"takeoff_within_limits\": true, \"landing_within_limits\": true}\n```\n",
